  "_excluded": {
    "WASHBOARD": "NO washboards on this hull, and this is the load-bearing absence. The rig draws a deck margin alongside the house, but measured at the deck line it is 0.076–0.412 m wide (11 samples, y -4.95 → 0.99, widening only as the house nose narrows into the foredeck): a reveal between the house side and the covering board, not a strip anyone walks. It is that narrow by design — clampHW lands the house sides on the cap so the covering board reads as ONE unbroken line stem to transom. Consequence: cockpit and foredeck are separate walkable islands on the exterior.",
    "covering_board": "The teak cap outboard of the reveal is rolled and carries a toe rail lifting to 0.15 m forward of u=0.55 — a boundary, not a surface.",
    "house_interior": "Salon is modelled as an exterior volume only — no interior floor exists to walk.",
    "bridge_access_interior": "No ladder from the cockpit or mezzanine to the flybridge is modelled on this hull — the real route is interior stairs through the salon, which the rig does not build. The tower ladder (bridge → tower) IS modelled.",
    "foredeck_access": "Nothing in the rig connects the cockpit to the foredeck: no margin wide enough to walk, no ladder, no door in the house exterior other than the aft glass. Any walk-forward move a character makes on this hull has to be authored game-side.",
    "gear_above": "Outriggers, tower pipework, whips, radomes and rod tubes are gear over the decks, not surfaces. Rod points are ANCHORS.rods.",
    "topside_detail": "Hull windows, louvre vents and the boot/cove bands are paint and detail, outside any walkable surface.",
    "bridge_route_closed": "THE FINDING CLOSED: the interior companionway salon→bridge_sole is modelled (STAIRS.house_to_bridge) — the flybridge is reachable without a game-side teleport",
    "foredeck_route": "no exterior route cockpit→foredeck — the extractor finding stands (no washboards by design)",
    "below_aft": "the below flat’s aft end tucks under the raised salon — full headroom holds only forward of the trunk (authored abstraction, flagged)",
    "engine_room": "the machinery space lies AFT of the flat under the raised salon (y < 0.45) — dressed, never walkable; access is the cockpit sole hatches (extractor sole_hatches)",
    "rode_locker": "chain/rode stowage forward of y 4.50 in the forepeak — dressed"
  },
  "_confirm": {
    "cleat_identification": "All three CLEATS entries are read from unlabelled iron fittings (see each provenance). Positions are exact; the reading as tie-offs is the art side’s, and a gameplay ruling can demote any of them.",
    "upper_decks": "bridge_sole, aft_deck and tower_platform are included because they are real modelled surfaces with real dimensions. If gameplay only ever walks the cockpit, mezzanine, side decks and foredeck, the upper polygons are inert data — they are not a claim that a character can reach them.",
    "aft_deck_rail": "The 53′ CONVERTIBLE’s aft deck (z=4.66) carries NO rail in the rig — railH:0. Either it is an unguarded edge above the mezzanine or the rail is simply not modelled; a fall rule needs a ruling either way."
  },
